I was just playing Nethack 3.0.7 on my Atari ST a few minutes ago and had
the following strange thing happen.  All of a sudden, in the middle of my
game, I started tripping, stumbling, flailing, etc. for no apparent reason.
I didn't have any boots or shoes of any kind on and my dexterity statistic
wasn't particularly bad (12).  Anyone have an idea what might be the culprit
here?

(spoiler below)


Also, for amusement's sake, here's what happened in another game.  I was
on level 8 or so getting whaled on by a Mordor orc with 5 hit-points left.
The situation was as illustrated below:

        -------
        |.....o
        |....@|
        |.....|
        |.....|
        -------

Knowing that I couldn't successfully pray with 5 hit-points (one hit-point
too many!), I got this bright idea that I could move down (like so):

        -------
        |.....o
        |.....|
        |....@|
        |.....|
        -------

kick the wall, lose maybe 2 or 3 hit-points, pray and get them all back and
more.  Well, that was the first and only time I've ever seen kicking a wall
take off 5 hit-points or more!  That seems kind of bogus to me, since I
kicked the wall on purpose and I should have control over whether I kick
it with all my might or just moderately hard.

While I'm going, here's another doozy.  I'm in a big room fighting with
a dwarf, getting low on hit-points and figuring it's time to use my wand
of fire.  Here's the situation:


        -------------------
        |.................|
        |.................|
        |.......@.........|
        |......h..........|
        |.................|
        |.................|
        |.................|
        -------------------

I zapped the wand and it killed the dwarf alright, but it also bounced right
back at me and killed myself too.  I could understand if it bounced several
times, but it just bounced straight off the bottom wall and back.  I have a
hard time figuring out the rationale for that!  Does this follow any kind of
rule or is it just some more arbitrariness and my bad luck?

As you can see, it's been a long day ...

